Kendar DLNA music server
========================

This product bundles or depends on the third-party components below. Each is used unmodified (except JAAD, see below); versions are pinned
in build.gradle. The text of each licence is available from the component's own distribution (Maven Central
artifacts carry it in META-INF or in the source jar) and, for GeneralUser GS, in
src/main/resources/soundfont/LICENSE-GeneralUser-GS.txt.


Audio codecs (transcoding)
--------------------------

jump3r 1.0.5 (de.sciss:jump3r)                      GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL), v2.1 or later
    A pure-Java port of the LAME 3.98.4 MP3 encoder (https://lame.sourceforge.io, LGPL). Used to encode the MP3
    form of non-MP3 sources and rendered MIDI.

JLayer 1.0.1.4 (com.googlecode.soundlibs:jlayer)    GNU (Library) General Public License (LGPL)
    MP3 decoding (https://github.com/umjammer/jlayer, from JavaZoom's JLayer).

JOrbis 0.0.17 (org.jcraft:jorbis)                   GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL)
    Ogg Vorbis decoding (http://www.jcraft.com/jorbis/).

JFLAC 1.5.2 (org.jflac:jflac-codec)                 GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL)
    FLAC decoding (https://jflac.sourceforge.net).

Concentus 1.0.2 (io.github.jaredmdobson:concentus)  BSD-style licence (Xiph.Org, Skype Limited, Broadcom, Jean-Marc
    Valin and contributors; the licence of the Opus reference implementation)
    Opus decoding (https://github.com/lostromb/concentus). Ogg demuxing for Opus is our own code.

JAAD 0.9.4 (com.tianscar.javasound:jaad)             Apache License 2.0 (the original JAAD by in-somnia is public domain)
    AAC-LC decoding (https://github.com/Tianscar/jaadec, fork of JAAD, https://sourceforge.net/projects/jaadec). The
    jar is repackaged by the build (task jaadNoSpi) without its Java Sound service registration, and two classes
    are replaced by modified copies kept in src/main/java/net/sourceforge/jaad: aac/tools/TNS.java (the temporal
    noise shaping filter, a stub in the original, implemented after the FAAD2/ffmpeg algorithm) and
    aac/syntax/IQTable.java (table size fixed from 8191 to 8192 entries). Both files say so in their header.
    The MP4/ADTS demuxer that feeds it is our own code.

Apple Lossless decoder (org.kendar.dlna.transcoding.AlacFrames) is our own code, written from the public description
    of the format and the structure of Apple's open-source ALAC decoder (Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/macosforge/alac)
    and Peter McQuillan's Java port com.beatofthedrum.alacdecoder (BSD licence, Copyright (c) 2011 Peter McQuillan,
    all rights reserved; redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without modification, are permitted
    provided that the copyright notice, the licence conditions and the disclaimer are retained). That port was read as a
    reference and is not a dependency.

jaudiotagger 3.0.1 (net.jthink:jaudiotagger)        GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL), v2.1 or later
    Reading and writing audio tags.

Rendering of MIDI uses the software synthesizer of the JDK (Gervill, OpenJDK, GPL v2 with the Classpath Exception).

LGPL notice: the LGPL libraries above are included unmodified. Replacing one with a modified version is done by
changing its version in build.gradle (they are resolved as separate artifacts from Maven Central) and rebuilding
with ./gradlew build; the fat jar is only a repackaging of those artifacts.


SoundFont
---------

GeneralUser GS v2.0.3 by S. Christian Collins (http://www.schristiancollins.com)
    Bundled as src/main/resources/soundfont/GeneralUser-GS.sf2 when present (it is large and is not generated by the
    build). The author's licence permits use in software projects, including commercial ones, and modification of
    the bank or its packaging; it is reproduced in src/main/resources/soundfont/LICENSE-GeneralUser-GS.txt and must be
    kept with the SoundFont. Any other SF2 file can be used instead through "transcode.soundFontPath".


